A||||3||Gerald||How about a 4.3||||1||
Z||000000||Gerald||09-29-2001||09:23 AM||||I was thinking of ways to make my 87 coupe a little faster, but I gave up on the duke, POS. So I was thinking that a 4.3 would do real nicely. I am thinking a carbed engine is the way to go to avoid a massive amount of electrical probles which Im sure would ocure if I tried to make it fuel injected. Problem is that I have never heard of a 4.3 fiero. If anyone knows of one could you please tell me. I think my biggest problem is going to be mounting the thing.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ronnie||09-29-2001||10:17 AM||||I've often thought about that swap myself , but it would have to be installed using a V8 type kit because it was never used as a front wheel drive application(transversely mounted). So the problem with me on that is, if you've got to go to all that trouble , you just as well go ahead with the V8 instead.||||reg||6
Z||000002||Gerald||09-29-2001||10:59 PM||||Hey Ronnie, I kinda thought it would be like a v8 swap but I really want to beat rice at their own game. There seems to be a lot of races here that are restricted. No V8s aloud.Plus I want the extra room to work on it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||09-29-2001||11:19 PM||||There are a couple 4.3s running around. At least one on this Forum. I've always thought it would make a neat swap. The 4.3 in my Sonoma would almost drag my house off the foundation. The truth of the matter is that a 3800 is an easier swap. The trans will bolt right up, and several kits are already available. Horsepower numbers are similar.<BR>My 4.3 vibrates pretty badly, too. Pretty common in the earlier ones. Later ones have balance shafts.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
